a requires a novel DNM1-interacting protein, Net2p. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>309</fpage>&#x02013;321.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11179417</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal">Chen, H., and D.C. Chan. <year>2004</year>. Mitochondrial dynamics in mammals. <source>Curr. Top. Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>59</volume>:<fpage>119</fpage>&#x02013;144.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14975249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal">D'Andrea, L.D., and L. Regan. <year>2003</year>. TPR proteins: the versatile helix. <source>Trends Biochem. Sci.</source> <volume>28</volume>:<fpage>655</fpage>&#x02013;662.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14659697</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Dohm, J.A., S.J. Lee, J.M. Hardwick, R.B. Hill, and A.G. Gittis. <year>2004</year>. Cytosolic domain of the human mitochondrial fission protein fis1 adopts a TPR fold. <source>Proteins.</source> <volume>54</volume>:<fpage>153</fpage>&#x02013;156.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14705031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Fekkes, P., K.A. Shepard, and M.P. Yaffe. <year>2000</year>. Gag3p, an outer membrane protein required for fission of mitochondrial tubules. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>151</volume>:<fpage>333</fpage>&#x02013;340.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11038180</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Frank, S., B. Gaume, E.S. Bergmann-Leitner, W.W. Leitner, E.G. Robert, F. Catez, C.L. Smith, and R.J. Youle. <year>2001</year>. The role of dynamin-related protein 1, a mediator of mitochondrial fission, in apoptosis. <source>Dev. Cell.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>515</fpage>&#x02013;525.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11703942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Fukushima, N.H., E. Brisch, B.R. Keegan, W. Bleazard, and J.M. Shaw. <year>2001</year>. The