olume>:<fpage>359</fpage>&#x02013;373.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9786948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Holm, L., and C. Sander. <year>1993</year>. Protein structure comparison by alignment of distance matrices. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>233</volume>:<fpage>123</fpage>&#x02013;138.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8377180</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Jagasia, R., P. Grote, B. Westermann, and B. Conradt. <year>2005</year>. DRP-1-mediated mitochondrial fragmentation during EGL-1-induced cell death in <italic>C. elegans</italic>. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>433</volume>:<fpage>754</fpage>&#x02013;760.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15716954</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">James, D.I., P.A. Parone, Y. Mattenberger, and J.C. Martinou. <year>2003</year>. hFis1, a novel component of the mammalian mitochondrial fission machinery. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>278</volume>:<fpage>36373</fpage>&#x02013;36379.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12783892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">James, P., J. Halladay, and E.A. Craig. <year>1996</year>. Genomic libraries and a host strain designed for highly efficient two-hybrid selection in yeast. <source>Genetics.</source> <volume>144</volume>:<fpage>1425</fpage>&#x02013;1436.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8978031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Jensen, R.E., A.E. Hobbs, K.L. Cerveny, and H. Sesaki. <year>2000</year>. Yeast mitochondrial dynamics: fusion, division, segregation, and shape. <source>Microsc. Res. Tech.</source> <volume>51</volume>:<fpage>573</fpage>&#x02013;583.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11169859</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Karbowski, M., and R.J. Youle. <year>2003</year>. Dynamics of mitochondrial morphology in healthy cells and during apoptosis. <source>Ce